From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp: mark the CDSP FastRPC context banks dma-coherent

The compute context banks of the CDSP's FastRPC node are described
without dma-coherent. The CDSP accesses memory through these SMMU
streams cache-coherently: SM8550 and SM8650 already mark the same
context banks dma-coherent, and the Windows driver for this SoC turns on
IO cache coherency for the CDSP (EnableIOCacheCoherency=0xF in its INF).
Described as non-coherent, the kernel's cache maintenance on buffers
shared with the CDSP disagrees with how the DSP sees them.

On the Huawei MateBook E Go, user-space FastRPC from
github.com/quic/fastrpc then fails to load a skel library into an
unsigned PD on the CDSP (AEE_EUNABLETOLOAD while mapping the library),
0 of 4 runs passed, unless the listener buffers are plain malloc memory
or the dma-bufs are synced around every invocation. With the context
banks marked dma-coherent, the unmodified library passed 6 of 6 runs,
and QNN HTP graphs on the CDSP give the same output as Qualcomm's HTP
emulator for the same graph.

The ADSP's context banks are left as they are; nothing here exercised
them.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
@@ -6168,84 +6168,98 @@
